-- title:
--   Admissibility at the three-dimensional orthogonal type
-- statement:
--   Let $f\colon \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})\to\mathbb{C}$. Assume: (i) `WhittakerBlock.IsOrthFinite f`, i.e. there is a finite set $s$ of functions such that for every $k$ whose component at each finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ is $1$ and whose archimedean component satisfies $k^{\mathsf T}k=1$, the translate $g\mapsto f(gk)$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of $s$; (ii) every element $\varphi$ of `WhittakerBlock.orthSpan f`, the span of all such translates, is centre-finite, i.e. for each of the three operators $\mathrm{casimir}_1\varphi=\sum_i\partial_{ii}\varphi$, $\mathrm{casimir}_2\varphi=\sum_{i,j}\partial_{ij}\partial_{ji}\varphi$, $\mathrm{casimir}_3\varphi=\sum_{i,j,k}\partial_{ij}\partial_{jk}\partial_{ki}\varphi$ (right derivatives at the infinite place) $\varphi$ satisfies a monic polynomial relation; (iii) every archimedean-smooth $\varphi$ whose underlying function lies in `orthSpan f` is annihilated by $\Omega+2$, where $\Omega$ is the sum of the squares of `derivAction3` applied to $E_{01}-E_{10}$, $E_{02}-E_{20}$, $E_{12}-E_{21}$; (iv) `orthSpan f` is stable under `derivAction3` along every $E_{ij}-E_{ji}$, $i,j\in\{0,1,2\}$. Let $B$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-valued form on smooth functions which, restricted to `gKSpan f` (the `envelopingAlgebra3`-submodule generated by the smooth elements of `orthSpan f`), is linear in its first argument, conjugate-symmetric, positive in the sense $\operatorname{Re}B(w,w)>0$ for $w\neq 0$, and for which each $E_{ij}-E_{ji}$ acts skew-adjointly. Then the intersection of `gKSpan f`, viewed as a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule, with $\ker(\Omega+2)$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the admissibility statement for the three-dimensional type of the orthogonal group at the infinite place: the $(\Omega+2)$-eigenspace of the $\mathfrak{gl}_3$-module generated by an orthogonally finite, centre-finite function has bounded multiplicity, the analogue for the type $\Omega=-2$ of the corresponding statement for the trivial type. It feeds into [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_finiteDimensional_forall_mem_hull_of_rotationType_of_smoothingSubmodule`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_finiteDimensional_forall_mem_hull_of_rotationType_of_smoothingSubmodule), and is proved from the description of invariant symbols in [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.tmul_mem_span_invariant_mul_sup_span_diagCasimir_of_isHomogeneous`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.tmul_mem_span_invariant_mul_sup_span_diagCasimir_of_isHomogeneous).
